0:{"buildId":"7afh9cBoHBO9HIwX4Lcyt","data":[{"rsc":["$","$1","c",{"children":[["$","$L2",null,{"toc":[{"depth":2,"url":"#the-problem","title":"The problem"},{"depth":2,"url":"#what-ships-in-local-remote-execution","title":["What ships in ",["$","code",null,{"children":"@local-remote-execution"}]]},{"depth":2,"url":"#set-it-up","title":"Set it up"},{"depth":3,"url":"#install-nix-with-flakes-enabled","title":"Install Nix with flakes enabled"},{"depth":3,"url":"#pull-the-template","title":"Pull the template"},{"depth":3,"url":"#initialise-git-before-you-enter-the-shell","title":"Initialise git before you enter the shell"},{"depth":3,"url":"#enter-the-dev-shell","title":"Enter the dev shell"},{"depth":3,"url":"#point-userbazelrc-at-your-cluster","title":["Point ",["$","code",null,{"children":"user.bazelrc"}]," at your cluster"]},{"depth":3,"url":"#build","title":"Build"},{"depth":2,"url":"#adding-lre-to-a-project-you-already-have","title":"Adding LRE to a project you already have"},{"depth":2,"url":"#troubleshooting","title":"Troubleshooting"},{"depth":2,"url":"#faq","title":"FAQ"}],"children":[["$","$L3",null,{"children":"Toolchains and hermeticity"}],["$","$L4",null,{"children":"Your action ran on a worker and failed on a missing compiler. Here is why that happens, and how to pin the toolchain so local and remote builds hash identically."}],["$","$L5",null,{"children":["\n",["$","p",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Who this is for:"}]," anyone whose actions execute remotely but fail on the\nworker for reasons that never happen locally. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"What you'll have at the end:"}],"\na Nix-pinned toolchain that produces the same action digests on your machine\nand on a worker. ",["$","strong",null,{"children":"Time:"}]," thirty minutes for the walkthrough."]}],"\n",["$","div",null,{"data-prerequisites":true,"className":"my-6 rounded-xl border border-border bg-surface-elevated px-5 py-3","children":[["$","p",null,{"className":"my-0 font-mono text-xs font-semibold uppercase tracking-[0.12em] text-brand","children":"Before you start"}],["$","div",null,{"className":"mt-1 text-sm text-muted-foreground [&>p]:my-0","children":["$","p",null,{"children":["A cache serving hits to your build. If you don't have one yet, start with ",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/getting-started","children":"Getting started"}],"."]}]}]]}],"\n",["$","$L7",null,{"as":"h2","id":"the-problem","children":"The problem"}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"An action is a closed description of some work: input digests, a command\nline, an environment, and platform properties. If the compiler your command\ninvokes isn't in that description, the action is a lie: it works on your\nmachine because your machine happens to have the compiler, and it fails on a\nworker that doesn't."}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["This is not a Forge behaviour. It is what remote execution ",["$","em",null,{"children":"is"}],": the\nprotocol will faithfully reproduce whatever you described, and no more.\nCaching lets you get away with an under-described action because the only\nmachine that ever ran it was yours. Execution doesn't."]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":"Two ways out exist."}],"\n",["$","ol",null,{"children":["\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Make the environment part of the image."}]," Bake the toolchain into the\nworker's container, and route actions to it with the ",["$","code",null,{"children":"container-image"}],"\nproperty. Minimal, and it's what most fleets do first.\n",["$","$L6",null,{"href":"/remote-execution/containers-and-images","children":"Containers and images"}]," covers\nthis path."]}],"\n",["$","li",null,{"children":[["$","strong",null,{"children":"Make the toolchain part of the action."}]," Pin every tool at a\ncontent-addressed path so the toolchain itself is an input the CAS knows\nabout. This is Local Remote Execution, and it's the rest of this page."]}],"\n"]}],"\n",["$","p",null,{"children":["The second is strictly stronger: it gets you identical action digests\nlocally and remotely, which means a local build and a remote build share\ncache entries instead of each maintaining their own.\n","$L8"," is the conceptual write-up; this\npage is the mechanism."]}],"\n","$L9","\n","$La","\n","$Lb","\n","$Lc","\n","$Ld","\n","$Le","\n","$Lf","\n","$L10","\n","$L11","\n","$L12","\n","$L13","\n","$L14","\n","$L15","\n","$L16","\n","$L17","\n","$L18","\n","$L19","\n","$L1a","\n","$L1b","\n","$L1c","\n","$L1d","\n","$L1e"]}],"$L1f"]}],["$L20","$L21"],"$L22"]}],"isPartial":"$@23","staleTime":"$24","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L25","isPartial":"$@26","staleTime":"$24","varyParams":null},{"rsc":"$L27","isPartial":"$@28","staleTime":"$24","varyParams":"$29"}],"isUpgradeableISRFallback":false,"a":"$@2a","rootVaryParams":null,"needsRuntimeRequest":"$@2b"}
